  "text": "Silver Price in the 1960s\nBetween the first (1968-01-31) and last (1969-12-31) monthly observations available for the 1960s, the LBMA silver price went from $1.96 to $1.79 — a decline of 9% — with a sampled high of $2.50 (Jun 1968) and a sampled low of $1.56 (Jun 1969).\nYears in the 1960s\n1968\n1969\nSee today's live silver price on the\nspot dashboard\n, or\nshop silver bullion\nat Bullion Trading LLC.\nData retrieved 2026-09-26. Latest observation for this metal: 2026-09-25. The current month is provisional.\nSources, sampling and calculation methodology\n.\nPrepared by the\nBullion Trading LLC editorial team\n.",
